  "scope": "FE-2b internal fixed-input evaluation lifecycle, local cloud engineering only; QUANT_FIXED_EVAL_ENABLED stays off by default and no customer route is added.",
  "authority": "Owner explicit GO FE-2b and QR-2 S4-4/S4-5; periodic commit/push authorized. No target deployment, migration, activation, host/VPS work, private acceptance, Live, guard reset or Best Inputs apply.",
  "changes": [
    "IDs-only QR3/QR4 admission resolves immutable parent inputs, policies, cost models and complete comparison context. QR4 exposure/start/job composition is atomic; refused starts leave no orphan job or exposure.",
    "One QS scheduler claim and exactly eval:base plus eval:stress whole terminal evaluations. Verified dataset SHA is distinct from the bar-content digest. Live fences recheck authority and closure. No search, intermediate checkpoint resume or second attempt.",
    "Durable deterministic run/step/token units, active-launch exclusion and confirmed physical stop precede matching-unit cleanup and terminal parent writes. Cancellation remains available after owner/object revocation; unconfirmed stops retain STOPPING and the global slot.",
    "Cold recovery uses the existing exclusive offline guard, validates exact durable records and terminalizes fixed jobs. Pristine claim/mirror gaps, preparation, base intent/completion and pending stress are covered; committed base evidence is retained without retry.",
    "Closed read-only RR reader verifies immutable frozen object SHA, both exact steps and terminal envelope against stored closure identity. Historical reads do not require the current live engine; research/library APIs refuse fixed evaluations.",
    "Mixed-worker SERIALIZABLE transactions retry original SQLSTATE serialization/deadlock failures. Nested schema assertions preserve SQLSTATE while application schema refusals remain sanitized.",
    "Runtime dependency inventory includes all fixed-evaluation imports. The three pure library dependencies now shared by the runtime are removed from the multi-only list without removing them from its combined closure."
  ],
